            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "CI failure below. Unsure if this is relevant. On Linux so I can't try to re-create locally.\r\n\r\n```\r\nFAILED   1 test, listed below:\r\nFAILED   ...ild/Xtest_xdg_core/test/functional/core/startup_spec.lua @ 64: startup prevents remote UI infinite loop\r\n...ild/Xtest_xdg_core/test/functional/core/startup_spec.lua:64: Row 1 did not match.\r\nExpected:\r\n  |*^Cannot attach UI of :terminal child to its parent. (Unset $NVIM to skip this check) |\r\n  |[Process exited 1]                                                                  |\r\n  |                                                                                    |\r\nActual:\r\n  |*^                                                                                    |\r\n  |[Process exited 1]                                                                  |\r\n  |                                                                                    |\r\n\r\nTo print the expect() call that would assert the current screen state, use\r\nscreen:snapshot_util(). In case of non-deterministic failures, use\r\nscreen:redraw_debug() to show all intermediate screen states.\r\n\r\nSnapshot:\r\nscreen:expect([[\r\n  ^                                                                                    |\r\n  [Process exited 1]                                                                  |\r\n                                                                                      |\r\n]])\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t.../runner/work/neovim/neovim/test/functional/ui/screen.lua:918: in function '_wait'\r\n\t.../runner/work/neovim/neovim/test/functional/ui/screen.lua:541: in function 'expect'\r\n\t...ild/Xtest_xdg_core/test/functional/core/startup_spec.lua:64: in function <...ild/Xtest_xdg_core/test/functional/core/startup_spec.lua:57>\r\n```",
